Third-party material

The licence above covers this repository's own code and documentation only.

assets/published/ is not mine. Supporting_Data.xlsx and its README are the
published data of Lowe, A., Jones, L., Brennan, G., Creer, S., & de Vere, N.
(2022), Journal of Applied Ecology 59: 1484-1495, redistributed here under the
terms of their Dryad deposit, https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.rjdfn2z9s, which
places no restrictions on reuse (Dryad releases data under CC0 1.0). Cite the
paper and the dataset, not this repository, if you use them. The pipeline that
replica.nf reimplements is the authors',
https://github.com/colford/nbgw-plant-illumina-pipeline; no code of theirs is
copied here.

assets/plant_atlas_2020_gb.tsv is derived from Stroh, P.A., Walker, K.J.,
Humphrey, T.A., Pescott, O.L. & Burkmar, R.J. (2024), Plant Atlas 2020: native
status data, Zenodo, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11097371, under CC BY 4.0.
The attribution and the licence are repeated in the file's own header.

assets/reference/ holds GenBank records, pinned by accession and version in
assets/reference_manifest.tsv. NCBI places no restriction on the use or
redistribution of GenBank data; individual submitters may.

The taxon list of the National Botanic Garden of Wales Garden Explorer is NOT
in this repository. It carries no licence statement and, in the United Kingdom,
a sui generis database right, so it is not mine to sublicense. It was used to
build the reference library at one point. It no longer is: the library here is
built from Barcode UK and the Plant Atlas 2020 alone, so neither the list nor
anything derived from it is in this repository. docs/replica.md measures what
that costs.

Trimmomatic's stock adapter lists are not copied here either; the TRIM process
takes them by name from the installed package, which carries Trimmomatic's own
GPL-3.
